[[1,63,524288,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Disconnect the lower coolant outlet hose from the radiator and\ndrain the engine coolant.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Manually press the springs and\nremove the hose&#x27;s rapid attachment.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Recover the coolant using a suitable\ncontainer.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,524288,"<p>1. Undo the bolt (1a) for the inlet side driven pulley using the\ntools (1b) and (1c) for counter-torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.822.156.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1c</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.822.146.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Remove the inlet side driven pulley.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001770.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,524288,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the water pump (1b) complete with\nO-Ring (1c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001771.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,524288,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with O-Ring, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 2.3 ÷ 2.8</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001772.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,524288,"<p>Fit the inlet side driven pulley and fix\nit using the bolt without tightening it.</p><p>Connect the lower coolant outlet hose from\nthe radiator.</p><p>Refill the engine cooling system with coolant \n<a href=\"#/3024721\">0010T20</a> .</p>"],[1,63,1048576,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Disconnect the lower coolant outlet hose from the radiator and\ndrain the engine coolant.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Manually press the springs and\nremove the rapid attachment for the hose.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Recover the coolant using a suitable\ncontainer.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001773.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,1048576,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) of the inlet side drive pulley, using the\ntool (1b) for counter-torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.822.155.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Remove the inlet side driven pulley.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001774.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,1048576,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the water pump (1b) complete with\nO-Ring (1c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001775.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,1048576,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with O-Ring, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 2.3 ÷ 2.8</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001776.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,1048576,"<p>Fit the inlet side driven pulley and fix\nit using the bolts without tightening them.</p><p>Connect the lower coolant outlet hose from\nthe radiator.</p><p>Refill the engine cooling system with coolant \n<a href=\"#/3024721\">0010T20</a> .</p>"],[2,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Disconnect the lower coolant outlet hose from the radiator and\ndrain the engine coolant.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/769.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000041.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Manually press the springs and\nremove the rapid attachment for the hose.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Collect the coolant in a suitable\ncontainer.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002145.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) of the inlet side drive pulley, using the\ntool (1b) for counter-torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.822.155.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Remove the inlet side driven pulley.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002146.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the water pump (1b) complete with\nO-Ring (1c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002147.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with O-Ring, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 2.3 ÷ 2.8</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002148.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<p>Fit the inlet side driven pulley and fix\nit using the bolts without tightening them.</p><p>Connect the lower coolant outlet hose from\nthe radiator.</p><p>Refill the engine cooling system with coolant \n<a href=\"#/3024721\">0010T20</a> .</p>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/3025006\">1032B40</a></p><p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the side timing belt protection\n(1b).</p><p>2. Disconnect the electrical connection for the cam angle sensor\npositioned near the engine oil dipstick.</p><p>3. Undo the fixing bolts (3a) and remove the cam angle sensor (3b).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Timing sensor.</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024270\">K47</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002393.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,63,0,"<p>1. Undo the fixing bolts (1a) and remove the water pump (1b) complete\nwith O-ring underneath.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002394.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Replace the O-ring before fitting the coolant\npump.</p><p>Fit the coolant pump and tighten the bolts\nto torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.1 - 2.6</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Fit  the sensor and tighten the retaining\nbolt.</p><p>Tighten the sensor bolts to torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>CAM ANGLE SENSOR</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>0.9</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Connect the electrical connection</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Timing sensor.</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024270\">K47</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>Position the timing belt side shield and\ntighten the fixing bolts.</p><p><a href=\"#/3025006\">1032B40</a></p>"],[16,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Proceed with removal <a href=\"#/3025001\">1016A10</a> .</p><p>Disconnect the coolant outlet hose from\nthe radiator and drain the cooling system.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Recover the coolant using a suitable\ncontainer.</p></aside><p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the water pump (1b) complete with\ngasket.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2048476.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with gasket, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Cylinder head side) 2.3 ÷ 2.8</p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2048477.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,63,0,"<p>Refill the engine cooling system with coolant \n<a href=\"#/3024721\">0010T20</a> .</p><p>.Proceed with refitting <a href=\"#/3025001\">1016A10</a> .</p>"]]